From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:00:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fill s2b-efficiency: prove exists_handlerMachine (T1)

New helper modules under Games/Efficiency/ (namespace EffFill):
- Strings: log append, fixed-length decoding (fixLen), the k-way length
  selection (selLen, sumPoly), the canonical decoder (canonWord, canonFun),
  the activation loop over GGMRed.stateLoopFun (actLoop, RunsTo) and the
  machine glue (exists_splitMachine). First consumer of the GGM reduction
  module, imported directly.
- Handler: the raw function hRaw of a non-interactive handler, its
  polynomial time (hRaw_poly) and functional equation (hRaw_spec).
The initial state is carried in the advice beside A's advice. T1's sketch is
updated to the delivered proof.
